statementMd:
You are given a quantum oracle - an operation on $*N* + 1$ qubits which implements a function ![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/ca923da5e61e139eb5596a3b9e34cc7ef42d1433.png). You are guaranteed that the function $*f*$ implemented by the oracle is scalar product function (oracle from problem D1):

![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/2b31a0d1ff4af2d7c1af23391f540a01218c8fa7.png)

Here ![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/b27ec8b8056386de828da0df174348afa7d29512.png) (an array of $*N*$ integers, each of which can be 0 or 1).

Your task is to reconstruct the array ![image](https://espresso.codeforces.com/71fa108edb785ca9f729fa3cd5ad18556dd682e4.png). Your code is allowed to call the given oracle only once.

You have to implement an operation which takes the following inputs:

- an integer $*N*$ - the number of qubits in the oracle input ($1 ≤ *N* ≤ 8$),
- an oracle $*Uf*$, implemented as an operation with signature `((Qubit[], Qubit) => ())`, i.e., an operation which takes as input an array of qubits and an output qubit and has no output.

The return of your operation is an array of integers of length $*N*$, each of them 0 or 1.

Your code should have the following signature:

```
namespace Solution {
    open Microsoft.Quantum.Primitive;
    open Microsoft.Quantum.Canon;

    operation Solve (N : Int, Uf : ((Qubit[], Qubit) => ())) : Int[]
    {
        body
        {
            // your code here
        }
    }
}
```

